<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Promptuarium.Serializer</RootNamespace>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <!-- The library implements the experimental PromptuariumType control, so it uses it freely -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);PRMTSER001</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>Promptuarium.Serializer</PackageId>
    <Title>Promptuarium.Serializer</Title>
    <Description>A general serializer between .NET objects and Promptuarium trees in the PRMT:CFG1-LE layout: typed holders, byte[] as BLOB, no JSON in between; layering (Populate), records, attributes.</Description>
    <PackageTags>promptuarium serializer serialization configuration binary tree</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Still experimental (opt-in PRMTSER000); the format (SERIALIZER_FORMAT.md) is unchanged. Changed behaviour: a long, ulong or decimal that a FLOAT64 does not hold exactly (e.g. 2^53 + 1, long.MaxValue, a decimal with more than 15 digits) is rejected when written (NotSupportedException), instead of being stored changed or unreadable. New: [PromptuariumType(Utf8String)] (PRMTSER001) on a property of an IParsable type (e.g. IPAddress, int) stores its text (invariant culture), and on a class or a struct stores every value of the type as text, in collections and dictionaries too; a property of another type declared as Utf8String, which was rejected, is now stored as text. PromptuariumSerializerOptions.AddTextType&lt;T&gt;(format, parse) and AddBlobType&lt;T&gt;(toBytes, fromBytes) store every value of a type as its text (UTF8_STRING) or its bytes (BLOB). The text or the bytes must give back an equal value, or the value is rejected when written; a text or bytes that do not convert are rejected when read. Version, Uri (its original string), IPAddress and IPNetwork are stored as text by default (until now they were written as objects that did not come back, or not at all); a registration wins over them, and ClearDefaultTypes() removes them. The options can not be changed after they have been used.</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../Promptuarium/Promptuarium.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Promptuarium.Serializer.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
